Infrastructure Type initialization alone shall not create a deadlock unless some code
called from a  type initializer (directly or indirectly) explicitly
invokes blocking operations. The following code results in a deadlock using System.Threading;
class MyClass
{
    static void Main() { /* Won’t run... the static constructor deadlocks */  }

    static MyClass()
    {
        Thread thread = new Thread(arg => { });
        thread.Start();
        thread.Join();
    }
} Original author is Igor Ostrovsky, see his post here .

