Foreach uses Duck Typing Paraphrasing, or shamelessly stealing from Krzysztof Cwalinas blog on this. More interesting trivia than anything. For your object to support foreach, you don't have to implement IEnumerable . I.e. this is not a constraint and it isn't checked by the compiler. What's checked is that Your object provide a public method GetEnumerator that takes no parameters return a type that has two members a parameterless method MoveNext that returns a boolean a property Current with a getter that returns an Object For example, class Foo
{
    public Bar GetEnumerator() { return new Bar(); }

    public struct Bar
    {
        public bool MoveNext()
        {
            return false;
        }

        public object Current
        {
            get { return null; }
        }
    }
}

