{
  var divs = getObjectsByTagAndClass('div','popupDiv');
  if (divs != undefined && divs != null)
  {
    for (var i = 0; i < divs.length; i++)
    {
      if (divs[i].id == popupID)
        divs[i].style.display = 'block';        
    }
  }
} (utility function getObjectsByTagAndClass not listed) Ideally I'll find out why the same item is being inserted multiple times, but I don't have control over the rendering platform, just its inputs. So when debugging issues like this, remember to check for duplicate IDs in the DOM, which can break getElementById . To everyone who answered, thanks for your help!

