Because debug headers can override the operator new signature, it is best to use the ... signatures as a complete remedy: private:
void* operator new(size_t, ...) = delete;
void* operator new[](size_t, ...) = delete;

this can be prevented by making constructors private and providing a static member to create an object in the stack Class Foo
{
    private:
        Foo();
        Foo(Foo& );
    public:
        static Foo GenerateInstance() { 
            Foo a ; return a; 
        }
} this will make creation of the object always in the stack.

