You can also do a conditional check with parameters in the constructor, which allows some flexibility. public MyClass(object myObject=null): base(myObject ?? new myOtherObject())
{
} or public MyClass(object myObject=null): base(myObject==null ? new myOtherObject(): myObject)
{
}

As per some of the other answers listed here, you can pass parameters into the base class constructor.  It is advised to call your base class constructor at the beginning of the constructor for your inherited class. public class MyException : Exception
