    }
} I note that in your example you never made use of the extraInfo parameter, so I assumed you might want to concatenate the extraInfo string parameter to the Message property of your exception (it seems that this is being ignored in the accepted answer and the code in your question). This is simply achieved by invoking the base class constructor, and then updating the Message property with the extra info. public class MyException: Exception
{
